 "text": "Place-lore is the study of names and the stories tied to a landscape. Many European place-names have Celtic roots, such as those ending in -dunum, meaning fort or town, and those with nemeton, meaning sacred grove. The Celts saw a place as holy and tied to a spirit or tale. In ancient Ireland, remembering place-names was a duty of the poetic class, and poems often told the names of the land.",
